cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Closed-loop degradation of an int8-quantised neural controller
  on an unstable magnetic levitation plant
message: >-
  If you refer to this work, please cite it using the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Svyatoslav
    family-names: Nikulin
    affiliation: >-
      Ural Federal University, Department of Control Engineering
      (programme 27.03.04 Control in Technical Systems)
    email: svyatik.super@gmail.com
repository-code: 'https://github.com/Taraved'
abstract: >-
  An open hardware test bench and measurement protocol for quantifying how
  much closed-loop control quality is lost when a neural controller trained
  to imitate model predictive control is quantised from float32 to int8 and
  executed on a microcontroller. The plant is a magnetic levitation rig built
  around a pot-core holding electromagnet, whose field topology restricts the
  working air gap to 2-3 mm and therefore raises the unstable pole to
  88.6 rad/s, forcing a 1 kHz control loop. The repository contains the
  hardware design, the firmware, the simulation pipeline and a measurement
  protocol registered before the corresponding experiments were run.
keywords:
  - magnetic levitation
  - model predictive control
  - neural network control
  - int8 quantisation
  - TinyML
  - embedded control
  - ESP32-S3
license: MIT
version: 0.2.0
date-released: '2026-08-31'
